course: dictionary
lesson: 4657
title: Words for sounds
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe how something sounds. Hoarse describes a voice that is rough, deep and croaky, as if your throat is scratchy and sore.
explain: The example shows why a voice goes hoarse. «Shouting for a long time strains the vocal cords so they swell and the voice goes hoarse.» The clue is shouting: when you shout for a long time, your throat gets sore and your voice sounds rough.
explain: Other words around hoarse give clues too. A hoarse whisper is a whisper that sounds rough, so a character may be ill, tired or scared. Shout yourself hoarse means you shouted until your voice went rough.
fact: Hoarse means rough, deep and croaky, like a voice with a sore throat.
fact: People often go hoarse after cheering at a match, singing a lot, or having a cold.
fact: Resting your voice and sipping warm drinks usually helps it come back.
fact: «A hoarse whisper» can show that a character is ill, tired or scared.
fact: Useful phrases: a hoarse voice, go hoarse, shout yourself hoarse.
exercise: «Shouting for a long time strains the vocal cords so they swell and the voice goes hoarse.» What makes a voice go hoarse here? | Walking slowly to school | Reading quietly in bed | *Shouting for a long time | Eating cold ice cream
exercise: Mia shouted for her team all afternoon, and now she can only manage a rough croak. What does hoarse mean? | Fast and happy | Soft and tiny, like a feather | *Rough, deep and croaky | Loud, clear and bright
exercise: Grandad says he will shout himself hoarse at the match. What does this mean? | *He will shout until his voice goes rough | He will forget how to talk | He will sing a happy song in the car | He will whisper all day long
test: A character speaks in a «hoarse whisper» because she is ill. What does this tell the reader? | She has just won a prize | She is very rich | *She may be ill, tired or scared | She is laughing at a joke
test: Which helps a hoarse voice come back? | Shouting louder to test it | Singing for three hours without a break | *Resting it and sipping a warm drink | Eating a big bag of crisps
exam: Which sentence uses hoarse correctly? | She hoarse a cake for tea | *After singing all day, Ella's voice was hoarse | The hoarse dog ate its dinner quickly | The hoarse sun shone over the sea
